From: Jonathan Wakely <jwakely@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:18:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] doc: Remove stray period in middle of sentence

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* doc/extend.texi (Attribute Syntax): Remove stray period.

(cherry picked from commit cac865464423d9827bd9e261060f4146090b8267)
---
 gcc/doc/extend.texi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/doc/extend.texi b/gcc/doc/extend.texi
index 88159822fa11..a44e7965b90a 100644
--- a/gcc/doc/extend.texi
+++ b/gcc/doc/extend.texi
@@ -9838,7 +9838,7 @@ does not distinguish between types with different attributes.  Support
 for attributes in C++ may be restricted in future to attributes on
 declarations only, but not on nested declarators.
 
-@xref{Attributes}, for details of the semantics of attributes.
+@xref{Attributes}, for details of the semantics of attributes
 applying to functions.
 
 An @dfn{attribute specifier} is of the form
